course: dictionary
lesson: 9950
title: Words from places
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Look at the ending: -ian, as in Tasmanian, often means "from or about" a place. Tasmania is an island state in the south of Australia, so Tasmanian means "from or about Tasmania." «The Tasmanian devil is a small, fierce black marsupial» tells you the devil is an animal from Tasmania.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. Tasmanian can be an adjective, as in «Tasmanian weather», or a noun, as in «A Tasmanian is a person from Tasmania.» Ask: does the word describe something, or does it name a person? The sentence tells you which.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial» uses or to explain a second name for the same animal. The sentence also says it was, not is, so the animal is no longer alive. Clues like this stop you from guessing wrong.
fact: Tasmanian means from or about Tasmania, an island state in the south of Australia.
fact: A Tasmanian is a person from Tasmania.
fact: The Tasmanian devil is a small, fierce black marsupial that lives only in Tasmania.
fact: The Tasmanian tiger, also called the thylacine, was a striped marsupial that is now extinct.
fact: Many Tasmanian devils are sick with a face tumour disease, so scientists protect them.
exercise: «The Tasmanian devil is a small, fierce black marsupial.» What does Tasmanian mean in this sentence? | *From or about Tasmania, an island state in the south of Australia | A kind of cold drink | A striped dog from Africa | A large bird that cannot fly
exercise: «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial.» What does the sentence tell you about the Tasmanian tiger? | *It was a striped marsupial and is now extinct | It is a kind of cat from Asia | It is a bird with a loud screech | It is a tiger that lives in Tasmania today
exercise: «Most Australian mammals are marsupials, whose tiny babies finish growing in a pouch.» Which animal is a marsupial, according to the sentence? | A penguin | *The wombat | A horse | A shark
exercise: «A Tasmanian is a person from Tasmania.» Is Tasmanian a noun or an adjective when it names a person? | *A noun | An adjective | A preposition | A verb
exercise: «Taz of Looney Tunes spins like a tornado, but a real Tasmanian devil does not spin.» What is the difference between Taz and a real Tasmanian devil? | They are exactly the same animal | *Taz spins in cartoons, but a real devil does not spin | Real devils spin like tornadoes | Taz is a koala
test: «The Tasmanian devil is the largest surviving meat-eating marsupial alive.» Which word tells you the devil is still living? | largest | marsupial | *alive | meat-eating
test: A Tasmanian is a person from Tasmania. What is a Tasmanian? | An island in the Pacific | A kind of marsupial that is extinct | A zoo keeper | *A person from Tasmania
exam: Which statement about the Tasmanian devil is true? | It is a striped animal that is now extinct | *It is a small, fierce black marsupial that lives only in Tasmania | It is a cartoon character that spins like a tornado | It is a bird from Tasmania
